---
permalink: /palette.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
The ⌘K palette's search index: every page in the nav, plus each of its ## and
### sections with that section's text, so a search for "neurips" lands on the
section that mentions it rather than only on the page.

Read from page source, the same way md/ does, rather than from rendered HTML.
That is why this file is named 0-palette.json. Jekyll renders pages in order of
file name, and once a page has rendered, site.pages hands back its HTML in place
of its Markdown; no heading survives that as a "## " line. The leading 0 sorts
this ahead of every page it reads. Named palette.json, it silently lost the
sections of every page that sorts before "p" (Experience, the homepage).
The homepage goes through home-prose.html for the same reason md/index.html
does: its raw source carries the Now widget's include tag, which is not text.

Anchors are not computed here. Liquid has no regex, and kramdown's id rule
(strip leading non-letters, drop anything outside [A-Za-z0-9 -], spaces to
hyphens) needs one; palette.js derives them from the heading text instead.

Deliberately absent: /resume. It is a private link handed out by hand, and
anything listed here is one keystroke from every visitor.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture home_src -%}{% include home-prose.html %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign paths = "index.md" | split: "," -%}
{%- for nav in site.pagelist -%}
  {%- assign nav_path = nav.url | append: ".md" -%}
  {%- assign paths = paths | push: nav_path -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign sep = "" -%}
[
{%- for path in paths -%}
  {%- assign p = site.pages | where: "path", path | first -%}
  {%- if p == nil -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if path == "index.md" -%}
    {%- assign src = home_src -%}
    {%- assign ptitle = "Home" -%}
    {%- assign pdesc = site.description -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign src = p.content -%}
    {%- assign ptitle = p.title -%}
    {%- assign pdesc = p.description -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign purl = p.url | relative_url -%}
  {{ sep }}
  {"type":"page","title":{{ ptitle | jsonify }},"url":{{ purl | jsonify }},"text":{{ pdesc | jsonify }}}
  {%- assign sep = "," -%}

  {%- comment -%} The Now section lives in an include, so the source never shows its heading. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if path == "index.md" -%}
  ,{"type":"section","page":"Home","title":"Right Now","url":{{ purl | jsonify }},"anchor":"right-now-","text":"What I'm listening to, reading, watching and playing right now. Music, books, films, games, chess."}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} A trailing h1 closes the last section, so the loop never has to. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign lines = src | remove: "[← Back to Home](/)" | append: "
# end" | newline_to_br | split: "<br />" -%}
  {%- assign heading = "" -%}
  {%- assign buf = "" -%}
  {%- for raw in lines -%}
    {%- assign line = raw | strip -%}
    {%- assign h3 = line | slice: 0, 4 -%}
    {%- assign h2 = line | slice: 0, 3 -%}
    {%- assign h1 = line | slice: 0, 2 -%}
    {%- assign next = nil -%}
    {%- if h3 == "### " -%}{%- assign next = line | remove_first: "### " -%}
    {%- elsif h2 == "## " -%}{%- assign next = line | remove_first: "## " -%}
    {%- elsif h1 == "# " -%}{%- assign next = "" -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if next != nil -%}
      {%- if heading != "" -%}
        {%- assign htext = heading | markdownify | strip_html | strip -%}
        {%- assign btext = buf | markdownify | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | strip | truncate: 900 -%}
        ,{"type":"section","page":{{ ptitle | jsonify }},"title":{{ htext | jsonify }},"url":{{ purl | jsonify }},"text":{{ btext | jsonify }}}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign heading = next | default: "" -%}
      {%- assign buf = "" -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- capture buf -%}{{ buf }}{{ raw }}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
